{"schema": 2, "id": "ruler-YUA", "title": "Yuan", "label": "Yuan", "description": "monnaie officielle de la république populaire de Chine", "extract": "Le yuan, appelé officiellement renminbi et surnommé kuai, est la devise nationale de la république populaire de Chine à l'exception des régions administratives spéciales de Hong Kong et de Macao qui possèdent leurs propres devises. Selon la norme internationale des codes des monnaies, la devise chinoise est désignée par CNY.", "type": "ruler", "typeLabel": "Souveraineté", "continents": ["Asie"], "epochs": ["moyen-age"], "from": 1272, "to": 1368, "itemCount": 172, "items": ["Aigun", "Alchuka", "Amdo", "Andong", "Anqing", "Barguzinsky", "Beijing", "Bhutan", "Bozhou", "Chahar", "Changsha", "Changzhi", "Chaozhou", "Chara", "Chengde", "Chenzhou", "Cicigar", "Dali", "Dalian", "Daming", "Dangla", "Datong", "Dege", "Dehong", "Dorno Govi", "Dornod", "Ejin", "Ereen", "Fengyang", "Fengyuan", "Fuyang", "Fuzhou", "Gaizhou", "Gansu", "Ganzhou", "Govi", "Govi Altay", "Guangnan", "Guangxi", "Guangzhou"], "source": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yuan", "articleLicense": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "image": "", "imageCredit": {"filename": "10_Yuan_-_Bank_of_Communications_(1941)_Japanese-controlled_area_issue_02.jpg", "artist": "The Bank of Communications", "license": "Public domain", "licenseUrl": "", "credit": "CHINA - REPUBLIC - Chinese Banks - Bank of Communications . (Banknote.ws)", "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:10_Yuan_-_Bank_of_Communications_(1941)_Japanese-controlled_area_issue_02.jpg"}, "revision": "", "sha256": "a83ad5abccb2ed38479f38508dfab391584fa261842e500f8ce61cd227eb7da5"}